<h2 id="how-the-quickbooks-sync-works">How the QuickBooks sync works</h2>
<p>Each company connects its own QuickBooks Online account. Every job becomes a sub-customer in the right company's books. When an invoice or a subcontractor bill is approved in the platform, it is pushed to QuickBooks with the right cost code, so nobody retypes it. QuickBooks stays the source of truth for cost codes.</p>
<h2 id="controls-that-save-money">Controls that save money</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Payment guard: no payment to a subcontractor with an unsigned contract or expired insurance.</li>
  <li>Approvals: bills and change orders need sign-off before they hit the books.</li>
  <li>Audit log: every change shows who made it and when.</li>
  <li>Money handled exactly: amounts stored as exact decimals, so totals always match QuickBooks.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="email-that-files-itself">Email that files itself</h2>
<p>Bids and supplier invoices usually arrive at shared inboxes. Connecting those inboxes through <a href="/integrations/microsoft-365-outlook">Microsoft 365</a> lets the platform pick up a bid or a bill and attach it to the right job and company for someone to review.</p>
